@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5080/api/v1
# One request per endpoint. Every mutating call after login needs the cookie the login set and the
# csrf_token it returned in X-CSRF-Token. Run `urlog user create --db data/metadata.db --name alice --admin` first.
# The error paths: a wrong password is 401 with the same body as an unknown name; a 6th login attempt from one
# address inside a minute is 429 with Retry-After; a case the caller is not a member of is 404 on every route.

### Login (sets the urlog_session cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "alice", "password": "correct horse battery staple" }

### Who am I (also returns the CSRF token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Users (admin): list
GET {{baseUrl}}/users

### Users (admin): create
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "name": "bob", "password": "another long password", "role": "analyst" }

### Users (admin): one
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/2

### Users (admin): role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/2/role
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "role": "admin" }

### Users (admin): unlock early
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/2/unlock
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Users (admin): set a new password (ends the user's sessions)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/2/password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "password": "yet another long password" }

### Cases: mine
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases

### Cases: create (the caller becomes owner)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "name": "incident 1" }

### Cases: one (404 unless a member)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1

### Cases: members
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/members

### Cases: fields for autocomplete (the catalog, this case's statistics, its span)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/fields

### Cases: share (owner)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/members
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "user": "bob", "role": "ro" }

### Cases: change a member's role (owner)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/members/2
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "role": "rw" }

### Cases: unshare (owner)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/members/2
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Admin: every case's metadata and members (never events)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/cases

### Admin: grant membership on any case (audited in the case's trail, by_admin: true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/cases/1/members
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "user": "alice", "role": "ro" }

### Admin: change a member's role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/cases/1/members/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "role": "rw" }

### Admin: remove a member
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/cases/1/members/1
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Upload: what the server speaks (tus 1.0: creation, termination, checksum, expiration)
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads

### Upload: create (owner or rw). Upload-Metadata is "key base64(value)" pairs: filename (required), host, timezone, year, nginx_log_format
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads
Tus-Resumable: 1.0.0
Upload-Length: 11
Upload-Metadata: filename YWNjZXNzLmxvZw==,host d2ViLTAx
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Upload: how far it is (the id is the last segment of the Location the create answered).
### Urlog-Upload-State is the state; "finalising" with Upload-Offset = Upload-Length means all bytes are stored and the record is pending
HEAD {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads/{{upload}}
Tus-Resumable: 1.0.0

### Upload: a chunk at the current offset; the last one answers after intake has recorded the file.
### 503 with Retry-After: the bytes are stored and the metadata store is busy; the record follows, ask HEAD and send nothing again
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads/{{upload}}
Tus-Resumable: 1.0.0
Upload-Offset: 0
Content-Type: application/offset+octet-stream
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

hello world

### Upload: what became of it (state, offset, file id, SHA-256, job id)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads/{{upload}}

### Upload: give up an unfinished one
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads/{{upload}}
Tus-Resumable: 1.0.0
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Search: the first request answers as a stream of events (meta, then histogram, page and counts as each is ready, then done).
### No range: the case's recorded span. No tz: UTC. A member the route does not know is refused.
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/search
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{"query": "src_ip=10.0.0.5 status=404", "from": "-7d@d", "tz": "Europe/Bucharest"}

### Search: the next page (the cursor is the page event's "next"; the query text is that of the first request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/search
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{"query": "src_ip=10.0.0.5 status=404", "cursor": "{{cursor}}"}

### Search: the result as a file, csv or json (one object a line), up to the export limit.
### formula_guard=true (csv only) prefixes cells a spreadsheet would read as a formula and says so in the first line
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/search/export?format=csv&query=src_ip%3D10.0.0.5%20%7C%20table%20_time%20user.name%20message

### Raw SQL: one table of the route's case; a refused text answers 400 with the gate's reason
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/sql
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{"sql": "SELECT host, count() AS c FROM events_v GROUP BY host ORDER BY c DESC"}

### Raw SQL: the result as a file
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/sql/export?format=json&sql=SELECT%20host%2C%20count()%20FROM%20events_v%20GROUP%20BY%20host

### A user changes their own password: every other session of the user ends. Counted by the login throttle.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "current_password": "correct horse battery staple", "new_password": "an entirely different passphrase" }

### Case dashboard: counts, flags, the queue, hosts, span, statistics state, disk use. No file list.
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/dashboard

### Lifecycle (owner): close, reopen. A refusal is 409 with the reason.
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/close
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/reopen
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Lifecycle (owner): archive a closed case, re-import an archived one. 202 with the task; the runner does the work.
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/archive
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/reimport
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Lifecycle (owner): soft-delete, confirmed by typing the name of the case exactly
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/delete
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "name": "incident 1" }

### The caller's own soft-deleted cases, with the day their purge falls due
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases?state=deleted

### Lifecycle (owner): restore a soft-deleted case to the state it was deleted in
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/restore
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Admin: purge a soft-deleted case. With two-person approval on this leaves a request ...
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/cases/1/purge
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### ... that another administrator confirms
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/cases/1/purge/confirm
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Hosts: list with their totals; create
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/hosts

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/hosts
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "name": "web-02", "timezone": "Europe/Bucharest", "source_options": { "nginx.log_format": "combined" } }

### Hosts: change the name, the zone or the default source options. If-Match is the host's version.
### Without confirm=true a change that would parse files again answers with their number and bytes and changes nothing.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/hosts/1?confirm=true
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
If-Match: "1"

{ "timezone": "Europe/Bucharest" }

### Hosts: merge host 2 into host 1. Rows keep the host they were written with; nothing is parsed again.
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/hosts/2/merge
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
If-Match: "1"

{ "into": 1 }

### Files: a page (after, limit up to 500), filtered by host, unassigned, state, kind, source, parent, pattern, extension, stale, q
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/files?limit=100&unassigned=true

### Files: one record in full; its ETag is the version a change names
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/files/1

### Files: host, zone, year of one file. 202 with the parse it queued. confirm_host accepts an inferred host as it is.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/files/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
If-Match: "1"

{ "host": "web-02", "timezone": "Europe/Bucharest", "year": 2026 }

### Files: override the source and its options; the detection result stays on the record. DELETE clears it.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/files/1/override
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
If-Match: "2"

{ "source": "nginx", "options": { "nginx.log_format": "$remote_addr [$time_local] \"$request\" $status" } }

### Files, bulk: give a host to the files a path pattern selects. This call changes nothing and answers the
### number of files, what would be parsed again and a digest ...
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/files/assign-host
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "pattern": "bundle.zip!web-02/**", "host": "web-02" }

### ... and this one makes the change: the same body, confirm=true, the digest in If-Match. At most 1,000 files
### a call; a larger selection is walked with "after_id" and "limit" in the body.
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/files/assign-host?confirm=true
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
If-Match: "{{digest}}"

{ "pattern": "bundle.zip!web-02/**", "host": "web-02" }

### Files, bulk: override the files of one extension and detector result (previewed and confirmed the same way)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/files/override
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "match": { "extension": "log", "detected_source": "generic" }, "source": "nginx", "options": { "nginx.log_format": "combined" } }

### Files, bulk: detect again the files a newer detector could send to a parser (or "file_ids": [..])
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/files/redetect
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "stale": true }

### Jobs: newest first (before, limit, state, file); one job with its progress and its reason
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/jobs?state=failed

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/jobs/1

### Jobs: cancel one that waits; queue the work of a failed or cancelled one again
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/jobs/2/cancel
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/jobs/2/retry
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
